  "findings": [
    "All three public RPCs require non-null auth.uid() equal to p_expected_user_id. Context additionally requires an Agreement where the actor is a party and matching group membership.",
    "Send locks account+request with pg_advisory_xact_lock and locks the group row. Existing sender+request returns its original receipt; different group or body raises GROUP_MESSAGE_KEY_REUSED.",
    "New send requires current membership/send permission and closure/safety barriers. The original body is stored with SHA-256 of its UTF-8 bytes; sequence and immutable visibility rows are committed in the same transaction.",
    "Recovery is a separate STABLE read bound to group+sender+request; its own body and receipt helper contain no send invocation or DML. The client validates account, group, client request and bodySha256 before accepting a receipt.",
    "Private group tables have no observed direct read/write grants for API roles. Deliberate public SECURITY DEFINER entry points have owner postgres and fixed pg_catalog search_path; internal group helpers are not callable by API roles.",
    "Client draft recovery remains compatible with the unchanged four-field journal and these current server contracts. No server migration is required for the reviewed client-only change."
  ],
